meta {
  name: Get User by ID (Other User - Error Canary)
  type: graphql
  seq: 52
}

post {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}
  body: graphql
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}
}

body:graphql {
  query GetUserOtherIdCustomerToken($id: ID!) {
    user(id: $id) {
      id
      email
      isActive
    }
  }
}

body:graphql:vars {
  {
    "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003"
  }
}

docs {
  Regression canary: user(id) queried with a customer-group token where the requested id belongs to a different user.
  ACCESS_TOKEN must belong to a regular customer whose userId is NOT "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003".
  Expected: null (not a GraphQL error) — resolver returns null to prevent user enumeration (CWE-203 anti-pattern guard).
  The resolver silently returns null for non-owner, non-management callers instead of throwing ForbiddenError.
  Guard under test: owner-or-management null-return in Query.user resolver.
  Schema: apps/user-service/src/graphql/schema.ts:Query.user
}
